__pycache__/
*.pyc
.env
.git/
.claude/

# Runtime/generated data - never bake this into the image. The app already
# handles a missing data/ directory gracefully (load_dashboard_data()
# returns {} if fleet_today.json isn't there yet), and the real content
# here is live client fleet data (positions, plates, tampering reports for
# GTL/AGL/ADT) that must never end up as a permanent layer in a Docker Hub
# image, public or private. The container gets this data at runtime via
# the mounted/mapped data/ volume and the daily import, not at build time.
data/

# Committed as a LOCAL DEV FALLBACK ONLY (see users.py's docstring) - real
# password hashes, must never ship inside a distributed image either.
database/users.json
# Runtime-written override file (see permissions.py) - same reasoning,
# and it's regenerated on demand anyway.
database/role_panels.json

# Test/dev-only files with no reason to ship in a production image.
# NOT scripts/ - scripts/init_db.py and scripts/export_sheets_to_mysql.py
# are meant to be run via `docker exec` on the deployed container itself
# (see DEPLOY.md), so they need to actually be in the image.
test_*.py
docs/
*.md
